HUMAN-EFFECT / REPORTING

Human-Effect Closure is CURRENT as a cross-cutting RULE/CONTRACT composition over existing owners. This candidate does
not invent a standalone SchemaID merely because the rule has a name.

RelationalInfluenceMaterialityPolicy/v1 preserves materiality, persistence, affected-domain, justified-baseline and
currentness semantics. Missing/stale/conflicting materiality evidence is non-PASS for a NON_MATERIAL claim.

Protected-reporting state is separate from allegation merits. Non-corroboration, error, withdrawal or unsupported merits
do not by themselves prove bad faith. Reporting creates no punishment authority and no blanket immunity. Direct and
indirect retaliation remain reviewable.

CROSS-SUBSYSTEM / CREDENTIAL / JUSTICE RETENTION

CausalClosureReceipt reuses the existing P024 causal-safety owner and canonical evidence/provenance artifacts. Lawful
erasure preserves only lawful minimum tombstone/surrogate state and revalidates dependents.

Credential states distinguish INVALID, REVOKED, EXPIRED, STALE, UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE and VERIFIER_UNKNOWN/UNKNOWN.
Unsupported/verifier-unknown is non-PASS, not INVALID and not PASS.

Urgent-preservation expiry invalidates retry/failover/queue replay until fresh current authority/evaluation. Uncertain
prior external effect preserves PARTIAL_EFFECT / OUTCOME_UNKNOWN and requires reconciliation before unsafe replay.

